    "text": {
     "en": "In India, many rivers, mountains and forests are considered sacred. The Ganga, Kaveri and Godavari are worshipped. The Himalayas and places like Kailash are revered.\nPilgrimages are journeys to holy places such as Varanasi, Rameswaram, Mecca, Bodh Gaya and Amritsar. People of all faiths visit sacred sites.\nSacred places bring people together and encourage care for nature."
    }
